    content: "Addiction is a battle fought not just with substances but with oneself. For those in Mumbai grappling with addiction, Releaf serves as a sanctuary, offering life coaching and sobriety consultations. At the heart of this initiative is Rahul Seth, a man whose personal battle with addiction has shaped his mission to help others reclaim their lives. Sober for eight years after multiple relapses, Rahul’s journey is a testament to the power of resilience and transformation.\n\n#### The Early Struggles: A Battle with Addiction\nRahul Seth’s story begins like many others—brimming with potential yet shadowed by the grip of addiction. Growing up in Mumbai, he faced the dual pressures of societal expectations and the allure of escapism.\n“I thought I had control over my choices, but addiction doesn’t just take control—it convinces you that you’re powerless to change,” Rahul recalls.\nMultiple relapses marked his early attempts at sobriety, each a painful reminder of how difficult the road to recovery can be. Yet, these setbacks planted the seeds of determination that would later grow into a life-altering mission.\n\n#### The Turning Point: Finding Strength in Vulnerability\nFor Rahul, the turning point came not with a grand epiphany but a quiet realization during his lowest moment. After another relapse, he made the bold decision to seek professional help and open up about his struggles.\n“It was the first time I truly confronted the pain I had been running from,” Rahul shares. This moment of vulnerability became the foundation for his recovery and eventual sobriety.\n\n#### Building a New Life: The Birth of Releaf\nSobriety wasn’t the end of the journey; it was the beginning. Rahul channeled his newfound clarity into a deeper purpose: helping others navigate the same treacherous waters he had crossed. In 2023, he launched Releaf, a sobriety and life coaching platform based in Mumbai.\nThe name Releaf symbolizes two things: the relief of finding freedom from addiction and the rebirth akin to leaves regrowing after a storm. With a compassionate and empathetic approach, Rahul built a community where individuals feel heard, supported, and guided.\n\n#### Overcoming Stigma: Addressing Addiction in Mumbai\nOne of Rahul’s biggest challenges has been combating the stigma surrounding addiction in India.\n“Many people think addiction is a moral failing, not a disease,” he explains. Through Releaf, he emphasizes that recovery is not about shame but empowerment. His workshops, one-on-one coaching, and group sessions focus on creating a judgment-free environment where clients can heal and grow.\n\n#### Why Choose Releaf: The Personal Touch\nUnlike generic sobriety programs, Rahul’s approach at Releaf is deeply personal. As someone who has walked the path of recovery, he brings a unique perspective to his coaching sessions. His methods combine proven psychological strategies with the insights he’s gained from his own struggles.\nHere’s what sets Releaf apart:\n- Empathy-Driven Coaching: Rahul knows firsthand the challenges of recovery and offers guidance without judgment.\n- Customized Plans: Each client’s journey is unique, and Releaf provides tailored strategies to meet individual needs.\n- Focus on Long-Term Growth: Sobriety isn’t just about quitting substances; it’s about building a fulfilling life.\n\n#### A Message of Hope\nRahul’s journey from relapse to resilience serves as a beacon of hope for anyone feeling trapped by addiction. His story reminds us that recovery is possible, even after setbacks.\n“Every day sober is a victory,” Rahul says. “It’s not about being perfect; it’s about choosing to keep going.”\n\n#### How to Begin Your Journey with Releaf\nIf you or someone you know is struggling with addiction in Mumbai, Releaf is here to help. Rahul Seth’s expertise and lived experience make him a trusted guide on the path to recovery. Explore one-on-one consultations, group workshops, and tailored life coaching programs designed to empower you to rebuild your life.\nContact us today and take the first step toward a brighter, sober future.\n\n#### Conclusion: Inspiring Change, One Life at a Time\nRahul Seth’s story is proof that even the darkest battles can lead to the brightest transformations. Through [Releaf](https://releaf.co.in/), he’s helping others write their own stories of resilience, recovery, and renewal. If you’re ready to begin your journey, you’re not alone – Rahul is here to walk with you every step of the way."
